# Reproducible with  python run_all.py  - 89.1 min on 6 CPU threads, the test photos
# scored once by step 7. So the inputs and the weights are not shipped:
data/                                   # the 94 MB tgz, 13394 photos, the 64x64 arrays (167 MB npz)
__pycache__/
results/*.pt                            # the two trained models, 500 KB each

# But results/ IS the deliverable next to this file: every number in RESULTS.md is in
# one of its .json files, and each of its 13 .txt files is the console output of exactly
# one command - the seven step logs and the combined run_all_log.txt that run_all.py
# writes and cross-checks, the four dryrun_* logs from the 2-epoch rehearsal (their
# commands are printed in RESULTS.md, since no run_all header covers them), and
# choices_report_log.txt from  python validate_choices.py --report.
#
# figures/ is 1.7 MB of PNG and is regenerated by steps 3-7, so it stays out; every
# number the figures are drawn from is in the JSONs, which is the order the code writes
# them in anyway (results JSON first, figures after, so a plotting failure cannot lose a
# results file).
figures/

# The previous run's artifacts, kept on this machine as the input to _compare_runs.py.
# Not shipped, and not needed: run run_all.py twice and pass the two directories to
#  python _compare_runs.py dir_a dir_b
_prev_run/
